# Sprite effects
@scenario tutorial_lesson_18
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide thoughtful]
ginger: Look at the edge of my sleeve. I'll switch the effect on and off so you can spot what changed.
[if !tutorial_still]
[set character.ginger.imageEffect pikupiku.lineboil]
[endif]
ginger: Look at the sprite outline.
[set character.ginger.imageEffect none]
ginger: Find the image-effect ID in this script. Set it to none to restore the original sprite.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: What is the clean baseline for judging a sprite effect?
> A different pose and new lighting. -> retry
> The same pose with its effect off. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: Keeping the input fixed isolates the change the effect makes. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Keeping the input fixed isolates the change the effect makes.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_18]
[flag tutorial_done_18]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_3]
